# Multitasking (X-Background=freeze; the launcher's APP-CONTRACT section 13): the harness plays the launcher with the
# toolkit's helper (apps/_common, cp0_app_lifecycle_lvgl.h). Hidden: not one flush, keys and taps ignored (a short Esc
# at the root would end the app); what was typed while frozen is dropped at show; shown: the whole screen repainted, the
# app as it was; close ends it through its normal exit (as Esc at the root). Without `lifecycle` nothing of this runs:
# the other scenes are the app as before.
title Template: hidden, shown, stale input, close
lifecycle
sizes 640x480 1280x720

shot before
expect visible
expect text "Device info"

# hidden: Esc, Enter and a tap reach nothing, nothing is drawn
hide
expect hidden
key esc
key enter
tapxy 0.5 0.5
wait 400
expect nowrite
expect noquit

# typed while frozen (still queued when it comes back): dropped by the show
stale esc
stale enter
show
expect visible
wait 300
expect repaint
expect noquit
expect text "Device info"
shot after

# the app works as before: Enter opens Device info, Esc comes back
key enter
expect text "Row / target"
key esc
expect noquit

# a second round trip, then the launcher's close: the app ends as with Esc at its root
hide
show
wait 300
expect repaint
close
expect quit
